<title>CYPRUS: U.S. firm Kellogg to revamp Algeria LNG plant.</title>
<headline>U.S. firm Kellogg to revamp Algeria LNG plant.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has chosen American firm M.W. Kellogg to complete the revamping of the GL1/K Skikda liquefied natural gas (LNG) plant, the Middle East Economic Survey said on Monday.</p>
<p>MEES said two trains at the plant have been revamped so far and that Kellogg has been selected to revamp the remaining three trains and complete the work within a year.</p>
</text>
